I have, by the way, evolved a way to survive this,
but it involves YANIs anew with unexplored
repercussions:

To battle the dreaded P.R. Drop Dragon, the
adventurer steps into a convenient nearby
already-looted chest, grasps the chest sides with
her gauntlets of power, and, like the leader in a
championship level sack race, hops repeatedly at the
Prince Rupert Drop Dragon, attempting to avoid its
razor talons, its slashing teeth, to gain its rear
aspect. Having done so, with a mighty heave, she
lands chest and self upon the monster's vulnerable
tail, at the exact same time ducking down into the
chest and pulling the lid shut over herself with a
slam.

When the sounds of *ching*, *screech*, *ka-chang*,
*yeowch*, as nasty glass bits of defeated P.R.D.D.
embed themselves into the circumambient monster
swarm, die down, the hardy adventurer pushes up the
lid for a peek, and if all is well, she steps forth
in triumph.

With insufficient dexterity, the lid won't close in
time, and the chest will end up full of adventurer
soup.

With really rotten luck the chest will re-lock
itself as the lid slams down, and the dessicated
remains of the starved adventurer will be the noisy
rattling bit inside a beloved kicking toy for a
toddler giant.

xanthian.

The implications for adventurers attempting sack
races using bags of tricks, or cursed bags of
holding, just boggle the easily boggled mind.

Not much air inside an oilskin sack, either, I
suppose, if one should pull it up over the head to
take a breather during melee dancing at the sack
sock-hop.

Being grabbed up by a giant and tied to the end of a
staff, then shouldered and carried off, when
mistaken for a long lost bindle while snoozing
within ones protective sack might be problematic.

Falling into a pit, down a hole or stairs or
trapdoor, could also be "inconvenient" in really
nasty ways.

But what a great way sack racing would be to
traverse unharmed through a swarm of puddings or of
monsters of size "small".

Hop, hop, hop. Goosh, goosh, goosh.

Should this be restricted to characters with the
"jumping" intrinsic or jumping boots? Would using a
blessed bag of holding for your sack make you able
to jump really, really far, like a moon explorer in
stylish spandex armor?


